      "title": "Fairmont State University: All Jobs",
      "description": "tag:www.fairmontstatejobs.com,2005:/postings/all_jobs Fairmont State University: All Jobs 2025-06-19T12:04:38-04:00 https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/8382 2025-06-19T12:04:37-04:00 2025-06-19T12:04:38-04:00 Campus Police Officer <div>Supports Fairmont State University by establishing and maintaining a safe atmosphere for the faculty, staff, students, and visitors by providing police and security services. Patrols campus in vehicle and on foot daily and during special events. Enforces all laws, regulations, and policies as needed. Works independently on a day-to-day basis under the supervision of a supervisor, but with the ability to deal with unusual situations as needed.<br>General duties and responsibilities include but are not limited to:</div><ul><li>Serves as a preliminary and follow-up investigator;</li><li>Patrols campus checking buildings and infrastructure for security issues and deficiencies which make the institution vulnerable to criminal acts;</li><li>Patrols during special events, such as athletic events, concerts, etc. Directs traffic before, during and after the events;</li><li>Provides crowd control which can include managing large numbers of people;</li><li>Enforces all Federal, State, and Local laws, ordinances, and University regulations and policies;</li><li>Enforces campus parking and traffic regulations;</li><li>Makes arrests in accordance with departmental policies;</li><li>Investigates traffic-related and general complaints;</li><li>Testifies in court as needed;</li><li>Watches for hazards and other dangerous or damaging situations;</li><li>Administers first aid and provides or arranges necessary transportation;</li><li>Provides police escorts as needed to protect property or people;</li><li>Assists with the Fairmont State University Police Academy as needed; and</li><li>Performs related duties as assigned or as directed.</li></ul> Pooled Staff Position https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11673 2026-08-11T13:22:39-04:00 2026-08-11T13:22:39-04:00 Assistant Professor of Nursing <div>Teaching:<br>Participates in the development and evaluation of the ASN and/or BSN program<br>Develops, teaches, and evaluates assigned courses<br>Evaluates student performance on exams and course assignments<br>Evaluates student performance in the clinical environment; including skills lab and simulation lab<br>Assumes responsibility for serving as a course coordinator, as appropriate<br>Coordinates clinical rotation with clinical agency and clinical adjuncts<br>Teaches 12 credits per semester, includes theory, clinical, skills lab and simulation lab<br>Participate in ongoing course and curriculum revision<br><br>Service:<br>Provides engaged service at the programmatic, School, University and community levels<br>Participates in course and programmatic assessment activities<br>Participates in community and professional activities<br>Participates in student recruitment and retention activities<br>Advises currently enrolled and perspective students<br><br>Scholarship:<br>Maintains appropriate scholarly and professional development activities<br>Provides expertise in the area of medical-surgical nursing<br><br>Leadership:<br>Contributes to the continuing innovation and development of the programs in the School of Nursing<br>Participates in the assessment, evaluation, and accreditation of the School of Nursing programs and the University<br>Participates in, manage, or lead projects within the School of Nursing, and University as requested<br><br>Performs related duties as necessary and as assigned.</div> College of Nursing https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11724 2026-08-17T15:16:11-04:00 2026-08-17T15:16:11-04:00 Assistant Technical Director <div><strong>About the Position:</strong><br>The Assistant Technical Director is responsible for departmentally produced shows, including theatrical productions for Masquers, Town and Gown, and Academy for the Arts; musical productions for the Fairmont State bands and choirs, and special events, as required. The position provides scenic construction and technical support. Assists students in the execution of related projects. Assists the Technical Director in maintaining the Scene Shop as a safe and efficient working environment.<br><br><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></div><ul><li><strong>Production support</strong><ul><li>Works with the Technical Director in executing scenic designs for productions;</li><li>Works within the confines of established production budgets and productions schedules;</li><li>Works within University purchasing guidelines and coordinate with the Technical Director to obtain materials and services for the realization of designs and other production requirements.</li><li>Oversees the construction, installations, operations, maintenance and removal of the scenery and other elements that fall under the responsibility of the scene shop for each production.</li><li>Operates and supervises students in use of relevant digital technology, including AutoCad, LED/automated fixture programming, digital sound boardm and Qlab.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Student supervision</strong><ul><li>Guides students as to the proper construction and execution of projects;</li><li>Supervises and mentors students fulfilling design or other production assignments as it relates to the scene shop.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Scenic Construction</strong><ul><li>Works with Technical Director to determine proper methods for construction of scenic elements and create construction drawings as needed;</li><li>Carries out the construction of these elements in a timely manner;</li><li>Communicates any needs or adjustments regarding construction to the Technical Director</li><li>Works with the Technical Director to build, buy, modify or otherwise source suitable furniture and hand props for events within the production's constraints of time and budget; and</li><li>Assists the Technical Director in coordinating approved external scenic, furniture and properties rentals requests.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Shop Maintenance</strong><ul><li>Follows schedules established by the Technical Director for periodic maintenance of Scene Shop resources; and</li><li>Incorporates cleaning time into each day's schedule to maintain an uncluttered and safe work area.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Communication, leadership, planning, analytical skills, and decision making</strong><ul><li>Communication<ul><li>Provides frequent, constructive feedback to staff as appropriate.</li></ul></li><li>Leadership<ul><li>Ensures staff has the necessary knowledge, skills, and/or abilities to accomplish goals; and</li><li>Gives staff opportunities to enhance knowledge, skills, abilities, and/or experiences.</li></ul></li><li>Planning, Analytical Skills, and Decision Making<ul><li>Exercises good judgment and analytical skills as needed in making decisions and solving problems; and</li><li>Effectively identifies and addresses root problems, plan and coordinates projects efficiently and effectively.</li></ul></li></ul></li></ul> Dept of Humanities https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11810 2026-08-27T11:11:08-04:00 2026-08-27T11:11:09-04:00 Purchasing Assistant <div>The Purchasing Assistant supports the Director of Procurement and Assistant Director of Purchasing by coordinating essential purchasing, vendor management, and financial compliance activities. This role assists campus departments in navigating procurement processes and ensures adherence to federal, state, and institutional policies governing purchasing and vendor registration.<br><br></div><div>Work is performed under the general direction of the Assistant Director of Purchasing and within established policies, procedures, and regulatory frameworks. This position requires independent judgment, strong analytical skills, and the ability to interpret and apply complex procurement laws, rules, and guidelines.<br><br></div><div>The Purchasing Assistant interacts regularly with University faculty and staff at all levels, vendors, the West Virginia State Auditor’s Office, and the West Virginia Finance Division (wvOASIS).<br><br><strong>Essential Duties and Responsibilities:</strong></div><ul><li>Provide guidance to campus departments on purchasing procedures, procurement methods, documentation requirements, and policy interpretation.</li><li>Maintain tracking systems, logs, and records related to procurement workflows to ensure transparency, accuracy, and timely follow-up.</li><li>Coordinate vendor onboarding activities, including collecting, reviewing, and processing required documentation; resolve discrepancies with vendors and state agencies.</li><li>Provide administrative support to the Director and Assistant Director by compiling and maintaining contract-related documentation, monitoring key dates and deliverables, and assisting with the processing of renewals, amendments, and terminations.</li><li>Maintain and update vendor records within University and State financial systems, ensuring accuracy and consistency.</li><li>Process requisitions and issue routine purchase orders and service agreements; monitor status and communicate updates to departments.</li><li>Serve as a primary point of contact for departmental inquiries regarding procurement processes, documentation requirements, and transaction status.</li><li>Assist the Assistant Director in delivering training to campus departments on procurement policies, procedures, and best practices.</li><li>Serve as a resource to faculty, staff, vendors, and external stakeholders regarding procurement policies and processes.</li><li>Maintain and regularly update the Procurement webpage to ensure accuracy and relevance.</li><li>Perform other procurement-related duties as assigned.</li></ul> Procurement https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11828 2026-08-31T08:34:44-04:00 2026-08-31T08:34:44-04:00 Financial Reporting Manager <div>The Financial Reporting Manager supports the financial operations of Fairmont State University by collecting, reviewing and analyzing financial data for external and internal financial reporting requirements. This role assists in producing timely, accurate and compliant financial reports while adhering to federal, state and institutional regulations and guidelines, maintains strong communication and relationships with the campus community and key financial stakeholders.</div><div><strong>Operational Duties:</strong></div><ul><li>Internal Reporting –<ul><li>Assist with monthly, quarterly and year-end closing activities, including but not limited to preparing accrual entries, completing, reviewing and correcting journal entries, account reconciliations, and financial data to ensure the accuracy of financial information</li><li>Collect interim financial data, identify significant variances, interpret data, and collaborate with the Finance team to compile monthly financial statements</li><li>Create regular, recurring and ad hoc internal reports as needed to support university-wide decision-making</li><li>Internal reporting includes but is not limited to financial statements, capital project budget reports, fixed asset reports and proformas</li></ul></li><li>External Reporting –<ul><li>Collaborate with Institutional Resources to complete all required and requested external reporting in compliance with state, federal and higher education reporting requirements for various third-party stakeholders</li><li>External reporting includes but is not limited to Internal Revenue Service (IRS), National Collegiate Athletic Association (NCAA), Integrated Postsecondary Education Data System (IPEDS), Higher Education Policy Commission (HEPC) and the State of West Virginia.</li></ul></li><li>Audit Coordination –<ul><li>Assist Finance leaders with the preparation of the University’s annual audited consolidated financial statements, ensuring accuracy and compliance with policies, federal and state laws, Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP) and Governmental Accounting Standards Board (GASB) standards. Duties include but are not limited to developing workpapers, preparing schedules, creating and reviewing journal entries and collecting documentation.</li><li>Audits include but are not limited to National Collegiate Athletic Association (NCAA), Research &amp; Development (R&amp;D) and Single Financial Audit (SFA)</li></ul></li></ul><div>Process Improvement &amp; Systems Optimization:</div><ul><li>Policy Development: Work with Finance team to evaluate, update, implement and document departmental and university-wide financial policies and procedures.</li><li>Unit Collaboration: Collaboration includes but is not limited to, partnering with the Finance Team to ensure accurate and timely financial reporting and to ensure alignment between budget and actual reporting; and collaborating with departments across the university to promote clear understanding of financial data and processes</li><li>Improvement: Drive continuous improvement by automating manual processes and enhancing ERP system functionality in conjunction with the State of WV’s ERP system</li></ul><div><br>Other:</div><ul><li>Participates in other projects and performs other duties as assigned.</li></ul> Accounting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11842 2026-08-31T10:30:21-04:00 2026-08-31T10:30:21-04:00 Assistant Vice President of Facilities <div><strong>Job Description Summary:</strong></div><div>The Assistant Vice President for Facilities provides leadership and management oversight for all aspects of facilities, maintenance, grounds, custodial, construction, utilities, labor crews, and infrastructure. This includes the formulation of policy and standards, standards and procedures, safety practices, physical plant assessment, and occupational security standards. The AVP will foster a culture of process improvement and service orientation for the campus; evaluate and prioritize facility initiatives; and collaborate with stakeholders to further institutional strategic and operational goals to ensure the effective, efficient, and secure operation of all facilities. The AVP will be a creative and strategic leader, exhibit outstanding collaboration skills, and be an excellent communicator. The AVP reports to the Vice President of Finance &amp; Administration and Chief Financial Officer.<br><br>This position has been designated as essential. This means that when Fairmont State University is faced with an institutional emergency, employees in such positions may be required to remain at their work location or to report to work to protect, recover, and continue operations at Fairmont State University. <em>Fairmont State University is an equal-opportunity employer and is committed to enhancing diversity among its faculty and staff.<br><br></em><strong>Duties and Responsibilities:</strong></div><div>The AVP has responsibility for all aspects of the institution’s physical plant, trades and services, custodial, grounds, occupational safety, construction, and deferred maintenance program as well as all related departmental budgets and staff. Specific oversight functions include but are not limited to the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>The AVP of Facilities will integrate into the Universities culture as a collaborative service provider and partner within all levels of the organization.</li><li>Develop a service and student oriented mentality within the Facilities organization to support the strategic vision of the President and Board of Governors. Plans, sets priorities, identifies measurable outcomes, and oversees all major facilities functions and policies in alignment with the institution’s strategic initiatives.</li><li>Drives a team environment within the Facilities Department, keeping customer service, student support, and accountability as primary directives.</li><li>Establish and drive a maintenance and support culture to make all facilities and grounds a place of pride within the University community.</li><li>Develop a robust preventive maintenance life cycle plan and recommend funding streams for the replacement of campus infrastructure.</li><li>Facilitates professional training and development of employees; holds subordinates accountable for effectiveness, efficiency, and professional conduct; conducts effective searches by recruiting, hiring, training, evaluating, and motivating employees; participates in the administration of progressive discipline as needed; ensures good performance is rewarded; fosters an environment where all employees feel valued; promotes diversity, equity, and inclusion in all work units and decisions.</li><li>Coach and ensure team development and training to ensure that best practices are implemented and support a culture of quality customer service.</li><li>Oversees all capital construction and major deferred maintenance projects including development of RFPs, architectural design reviews, vendor management, quality assurance, system commissioning, invoice authorization, and warranty administration.</li><li>Provides Directors, Team Leads, and other supervisors with expert technical support and guidance relative to various building systems and equipment; oversees the utilization of the computerized maintenance management system including monthly reporting.</li><li>Recommends strategic and operational initiatives in support of the Strategic Vision which supports and advances the institution’s priorities.</li><li>Authorize and oversee the deployment, monitoring, maintenance, development, and support of all facilities-based assets for institution-wide needs.</li><li>Provide exceptional oversight with multiple vendors, including architects, engineers, and contractors, in coordination with all functional areas under the Facilities program.</li><li>Supports and helps with the administering of vendor, consultant, and service contracts and ensures that Fairmont State University receives the full scope of service detailed in contracts.</li><li>Prepare department annual budgets and administer funds according to budget approval.</li><li>Explore, evaluate, and prioritize opportunities for automation, efficiency, cost reductions, and sustainability efforts.</li><li>Collaborate with campus leadership in planning for disaster recovery and emergency responses.</li><li>Maintains awareness of changing trends and regulations that may impact the institution and recommends or take appropriate corrective action as required.</li><li>Other related duties as assigned.</li></ul><div><br></div> Facilities - Skilled Crafts https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11853 2026-09-03T13:02:19-04:00 2026-09-03T13:02:19-04:00 Admissions Counselor <div>Key Responsibilities:<br>1. Recruitment Strategy Development and Execution: o Develop and independently execute recruitment strategies for targeted student populations, including high school students, adult learners, and transfer students. o Plan and implement recruiting events such as college fairs, high school visits, and campus tours. These efforts will be guided by overarching enrollment goals and university priorities set by the Executive Director. o Evaluate the effectiveness of recruitment strategies within the assigned territory and make necessary adjustments based on data and feedback.<br><br>2. Student Engagement and Support: o Engage directly with prospective students and their families to provide guidance on the college application process, academic programs, and financial aid opportunities. o Provide one-on-one and group advising sessions for students, helping them navigate the admissions process, identify appropriate programs, and connect with necessary resources. o Serve as a trusted resource for students, offering ongoing support throughout the enrollment process to ensure they feel welcomed, informed, and prepared.<br><br>3. Admissions Operations and Event Coordination: o Working alongside the event coordinator-plan recruitment events within assigned territory, including campus visits, open houses, and information sessions. o Review and assess application materials for completeness, ensuring timely processing of student applications and corresponding communications. o Coordinate with academic departments and other campus offices to ensure that recruitment efforts align with institutional goals and meet student needs.<br><br>4. Strategic Reporting and Data Analysis: o Collect and analyze data related to admissions trends, student demographics, and recruitment outcomes to evaluate and adjust recruitment strategies within assigned territory. o Regularly report on progress toward recruitment goals, including analyzing application and yield rates, and presenting data to Admissions leadership for decision-making.<br><br>5. Professional Development: o Participate in professional development opportunities, including attendance at conferences and workshops, to stay current with trends in higher education, admissions practices, and student success strategies.<br><br>Admissions Counselor Requirements:<br>Experience in college admissions may be preferred.<br>Familiarity with college and university programs, majors, admissions requirements and processes, and scholarship and financial aid resources.<br>Excellent active listening, verbal and written communication, and interpersonal skills.<br>Strong planning and people reading skills.<br>Ability to multitask and stay organized.<br>Willingness to guide prospective students and families and provide ongoing support as they make important decisions.</div> Enrollment Management https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11658 2026-08-10T11:07:18-04:00 2026-08-10T11:07:18-04:00 Assistant Professor of History <div>The History Program at Fairmont State University is currently recruiting candidates for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of History specializing in Public History for a Fall 2027 appointment. The successful candidate for this position will teach courses in History as well as for the Museum Studies minor, with teaching responsibilities divided 50-50 between those fields. The successful candidate will also be expected to contribute to the History major and Museum Studies minor programs through curriculum development, promotion, recruitment, and growing partnerships with local, regional, and national museums and historic sites.</div><div><br>Preference will be given to candidates with broad experience in public history, with special consideration given to candidates with experience in museum studies. Additional experience in historical archives, oral history, material culture, historic preservation, heritage tourism, and/or folklore is preferred, as is expertise in Appalachian Studies. The ability to teach both survey and upper-level courses in 18th- and 19th-century American History is strongly preferred.</div><div><br>The required teaching load is four classes per semester. The successful candidate will demonstrate excellent, enthusiastic teaching and student advocacy; ability to work cooperatively and productively with faculty, staff and students; commitment to productivity and professional development; ability to use technology effectively in teaching, learning and assessment and active participation in department, college and community service.</div><div><br>Founded in 1865, Fairmont State University offers a proud tradition of quality education to approximately 3,500 students with undergraduate and graduate programs in various fields, including liberal arts, education, business, engineering technology, and pre-professional education. Fairmont State University sits in a beautiful, rural setting convenient in proximity to larger cities such as Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, and Washington, DC.</div> Dept of Social Science https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11677 2026-08-11T13:27:02-04:00 2026-08-11T13:27:02-04:00 Instructor of Nursing <div>Teaching:<br>Participates in the development and evaluation of the ASN and/or BSN program<br>Develops, teaches, and evaluates assigned courses<br>Evaluates student performance on exams and course assignments<br>Evaluates student performance in the clinical environment; including skills lab and simulation lab<br>Assumes responsibility for serving as a course coordinator, as appropriate<br>Coordinates clinical rotation with clinical agency and clinical adjuncts<br>Teaches 12 credits per semester, includes theory, clinical, skills lab and simulation lab<br>Participate in ongoing course and curriculum revision<br><br>Service:<br>Provides engaged service at the programmatic, School, University and community levels<br>Participates in course and programmatic assessment activities<br>Participates in community and professional activities<br>Participates in student recruitment and retention activities<br>Advises currently enrolled and perspective students<br><br>Scholarship:<br>Maintains appropriate scholarly and professional development activities<br>Provides expertise in the area of medical-surgical nursing<br><br>Leadership:<br>Contributes to the continuing innovation and development of the programs in the School of Nursing<br>Participates in the assessment, evaluation, and accreditation of the School of Nursing programs and the University<br>Participates in, manage, or lead projects within the School of Nursing, and University as requested<br><br>Performs related duties as necessary and as assigned.</div> College of Nursing https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11792 2026-08-21T12:13:45-04:00 2026-08-21T12:13:46-04:00 Presidential Events Office Assistant <div>The Part-Time Presidential Events &amp; Strategic Initiatives Assistant provides administrative, logistical, and operational support to the Director of Presidential Events &amp; Strategic Initiatives and the Office of the President. The position assists with presidential and university events, executive travel, purchasing, vendor coordination, communications, staff scheduling, mascot operations, and special projects. This position enables the Director to focus on executive-level event strategy, presidential priorities, strategic initiatives, and institutional relationships.</div><div><br><strong>Essential Responsibilities</strong></div><div><br><strong>Administrative &amp; Executive Support</strong></div><ul><li>Maintain calendars, event files, contact lists, spreadsheets, schedules, and planning documents.</li><li>Prepare agendas, invitations, itineraries, correspondence, meeting materials, and reports.</li><li>Track deadlines and follow up with campus departments, vendors, and stakeholders.</li><li>Organize electronic and physical records related to events, purchasing, contracts, and programs.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Event &amp; Program Support</strong></div><ul><li>Assist with planning and execution of presidential receptions, ceremonies, meetings, community-facing events, and special programs.</li><li>Coordinate RSVPs, guest lists, seating, catering, signage, supplies, event materials, and event-day logistics.</li><li>Coordinate routine event details with campus departments and external vendors.</li><li>Assist with setup and breakdown of events as needed.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Purchasing &amp; Vendor Support</strong></div><ul><li>Assist with quotes, invoices, purchase orders, receipts, and expense tracking.</li><li>Communicate with vendors regarding schedules, deliveries, event requirements, and logistics.</li><li>Maintain vendor records and assist with tracking contracts and deadlines.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Executive Travel &amp; Special Projects</strong></div><ul><li>Assist with hotel arrangements, transportation, itineraries, participant lists, meals, and materials for presidential and university travel programs.</li><li>Support conferences, retreats, and multi-day programs involving university leadership and participants.</li><li>Conduct research, gather information, prepare materials, and assist with special projects assigned by the Director of Presidential Events &amp; Strategic Initiatives or the Office of the President within the scope of the position’s responsibilities.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Communications &amp; University Representation</strong></div><ul><li>Assist with event invitations, promotional materials, social media, photography coordination, and event communications.</li><li>Coordinate with Marketing and Communications to support university branding and messaging.</li><li>Assist with scheduling and logistics for university mascot appearances and other university representation activities.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Staff Support</strong></div><ul><li>Assist with scheduling and coordinating student employees and part-time event staff.</li><li>Communicate assignments, schedules, and event responsibilities.</li><li>Assist with preparation and training of event staff.</li></ul> President's Office https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11823 2026-08-27T12:39:06-04:00 2026-08-27T12:39:06-04:00 Director of Global Education, Partnerships, and Immigration Services <div>The Director of Global Education, Partnerships, and Immigration Services provides leadership for the University's internationalization efforts through the development and administration of international student services, study abroad programs, global partnerships, and immigration compliance. The Director serves as the university’s PDSO and primary institutional resource for international students and scholars, oversees compliance with federal immigration regulations, advances global engagement initiatives, and fosters an inclusive campus environment that supports international education.</div><div>Reporting to the Dean of Honors and Global Education, the Director collaborates extensively with Academic Affairs, Student Affairs, Enrollment Management, Athletics, faculty, staff, and external partners to enhance international opportunities for students and strengthen the University's global presence.</div><div><br></div><h1><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></h1><div><br><strong>International Student Affairs</strong></div><ul><li>Facilitates communication among international students, faculty, staff, deans, and administrators.</li><li>Collaborates with Athletics to ensure strong support of international student athletes</li><li>Coordinates international students’ start- and end-of-term airport transportation with Athletics, Student Affairs, Academic Affairs, Enrollment Management and other campus constituencies.</li><li>Plans and conducts workshops on immigration-related topics for international students</li><li>Collaborates with student clubs related to international education</li></ul><div><br><strong>Inbound International Student Services</strong></div><ul><li>Works with the Director of Orientation to develop and implement international student orientation programs.</li><li>Provides pre-arrival information to international students</li><li>Provides resources and advice to international students related to obtaining a driver’s license, state ID, bank accounts, etc.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>International Education</strong> (Study Abroad Programs and International Partnerships)</div><ul><li>Promotes strong partnerships with counterparts at universities, state (e.g., Global West Virginia), and national organizations (e.g., the Association of International Educators (NAFSA), Fulbright, National Student Exchange, the Institute of International Education (IIE), etc.).</li><li>Develops and sustains robust relationships with international partner universities.</li><li>Maintains accurate and up-to-date records of all international partnerships.</li><li>Reviews and updates agreements regularly to reflect current terms and conditions.</li><li>Coordinates dual-degree and articulation agreements and maintains established relationships with global partners.</li><li>Facilitates enrollment in study abroad opportunities at Fairmont State for students at other West Virginia public institutions.</li><li>Guide US students through the study abroad application process.</li><li>Provides pre-departure orientation and re-entry support for study abroad students.</li><li>Assists in health and safety protocols for study abroad participants.</li><li>Provides emergency support and crisis management to students studying abroad.</li><li>Conducts risk assessments for study abroad destinations.</li><li>Facilitates faculty and student exchanges.</li><li>Plans and conducts workshops on cross-cultural competence for US faculty, staff, and students.</li><li>Acts as the primary liaison between the institution and international partners.</li></ul><div><br><strong>Administrative</strong></div><ul><li>Advises and assists international students regarding immigration matters, including, but not limited to:<ul><li>Maintaining visa status and compliance,</li><li>Visa renewals and extensions,</li><li>Changes in immigration policies and SEVIS alerts,</li><li>Preparing and submitting required immigration documents, and</li><li>Work authorization options (OPT, CPT, etc.).</li></ul></li><li>Supports F-1 and J-1 Visa status students as well as F-2 and J-2 dependents by maintaining a working knowledge of SEVIS and immigration regulations.</li><li>Oversees the generation, processing, and review of initial I-20s.</li><li>Serves as Fairmont State University’s Primary Designated School Official (PDSO) with the Department of Homeland Security.</li><li>Maintains Fairmont State University’s status as an SEVP-approved school and process I-17 for recertification.</li><li>Serves an Alternate Responsible Officer (ARO) for the WVHEPC J-1 Exchange Visitor Program Consortium.</li><li>Establishes institutional procedures to ensure institutional compliance with recordkeeping, retention and reporting requirements.</li><li>Oversees office budgeting and accounting.</li><li>Drafts and oversees processes related to global education.</li><li>Supervise student worker(s) and/or graduate assistant(s).</li><li>Engages in professional development to stay abreast of changes in the field.</li><li>Develops assessment processes to align with university’s strategic goals for global education</li><li>Prepares reports and updates for University leadership.</li><li>Supports grant-funded international initiatives when applicable.</li><li>Performs other related duties as necessary and as assigned.</li></ul> Academic Affairs https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11829 2026-08-31T08:35:31-04:00 2026-08-31T08:35:32-04:00 Manager of Grant Financial Operations <div>The Manager of Grant Financial Operations supports the fiscal administration and financial compliance of Fairmont State University’s sponsored programs including federal, state and private grants, contracts and awards. This role provides grant financial data to key stakeholders including but not limited to leadership, the Office of Sponsored Programs, Principal Investigators and all granting agencies/partners as required or requested</div><div>Operational Duties</div><ul><li>Manages the creation and closure of restricted funds within the University’s chart of accounts</li><li>Maintains restricted funds by tracking expenses, allocating payroll, updating budgets, posting journal entries and performs budget-to-actual reconciliations for receipts and disbursements</li><li>Prevents or corrects improper cost transfers and posting errors.</li><li>Completes month-end processes for restricted funds and runs monthly financial reports and schedules</li><li>Ensures a positive cash flow for restricted funds which includes but is not limited to timely invoices, completion of draw requests and required grant reporting</li><li>Collaborates with Finance areas and Human Resources to create, calculate and balance grant funded positions</li><li>Assists with the development of a streamlined cross-institutional billing workflow with Fairmont State Foundation</li><li>Works directly with Fairmont State Foundation to invoice for reimbursements and reconcile grant funded requests</li></ul><div>Audit and Reporting</div><ul><li>Assists with year-end processes and audit functions for the annual financial audit, including but not limited to timing functions to prepare schedules, completing calculation and analysis, creating and posting accrual entries and providing support documentation as requested by the auditors for restricted funds</li><li>Primary point of contact and coordinator for Research and Development audits</li><li>Ensures compliance with all financial reporting obligations</li><li>Assists with the completion of annual requirements for restricted funds including but not limited to Expenditure Schedule, Schedule of Expenditures of Federal Awards (SEFA) and Appropriation Requests for the State of West Virginia</li></ul><div>Process Improvement &amp; Systems Optimization</div><ul><li>Policy Development: Work with Finance team to evaluate, update, implement and document departmental and university-wide financial policies and procedures.</li><li>Unit Collaboration: Collaboration includes but is not limited to, partnering with the Finance Team to ensure accurate and timely financial reporting and to ensure alignment between budget and actual reporting; and collaborating with departments across the university to promote clear understanding of financial data and processes</li><li>Improvement: Drive continuous improvement by automating manual processes and enhancing ERP system functionality in conjunction with the State of WV’s ERP system</li></ul><div>Other</div><ul><li>Participates in other projects and performs other duties as assigned.</li></ul> Accounting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11845 2026-08-31T10:42:36-04:00 2026-08-31T10:42:36-04:00 Accountant II <div>The Accountant II supports the financial operations of Fairmont State University by performing various accounting, budget or audit tasks related to capital projects and fixed assets</div><div><br></div><div>Fixed Assets – Responsible for fixed asset process including but not limited to identifying, documenting, recording, reconciling, monitoring, and disposing of long-term physical assets, such as buildings, vehicles, equipment, and software</div><div>Maintain the fixed assets subledger and complete postings related to gain or loss on disposal of fixed assets</div><div>Collaborate with Finance areas to ensure timely and accurate reporting of fixed assets and ensure the fixed asset subledger reconciles with the general ledger</div><div>Collaborate with the campus community to ensure all assets are physically tagged and any variances identified through the periodic asset tag inspections are identified and addressed<br><br></div><div>Capital/Campus Projects – Responsible for capital/campus project process including but not limited to setup and closeout of project, documenting, recording, reconciling, and monitoring the financial performance of long-term projects like infrastructure, construction, and capital improvements including grant funded projects</div><div>Maintain capital project funds and complete postings related to Construction in Process</div><div>Collaborate with Finance area, project managers, facilities and operation teams to ensure timely and accurate reporting of capital/campus projects and ensure variances are identified and addressed</div><div>Post and process journal entries and adjustments</div><div>Assist with month-end and year-end closing processes, including gathering audit documentation and completing audit workpapers</div><div>Maintain compliance with institutional policies, fund accounting guidelines, and standard regulatory frameworks.<br><br>Post and process journal entries and adjustments</div><div>Assist with month-end and year-end closing processes, including gathering audit documentation and completing audit workpapers</div><div>Maintain compliance with institutional policies, fund accounting guidelines, and standard regulatory frameworks.</div><div>Other duties and projects as assigned</div> Accounting"
