    "https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11677": {
      "title": "Fairmont State University Portal | Instructor of Nursing",
      "description": "Fairmont State University Portal | Instructor of Nursing Skip to Main Content Office of Human Resources 1201 Locust Avenue, Fairmont, West Virginia 26554 Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Instructor of Nursing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Working Title Instructor of Nursing Type of Position Faculty Department College of Nursing Appointment Length Aug - May (9 mo) Tenure Status 3 - Faculty, not tenure eligible Academic Rank 4 - Instructor Is this considered a \"term\" position? No Benefits Eligible? Yes Published Salary F.T.E. 1.00 Grant Funded Position? No If temporary (or grant funded) position, indicate ending date Description of Job Duties and Responsibilities Teaching: Participates in the development and evaluation of the ASN and/or BSN program Develops, teaches, and evaluates assigned courses Evaluates student performance on exams and course assignments Evaluates student performance in the clinical environment; including skills lab and simulation lab Assumes responsibility for serving as a course coordinator, as appropriate Coordinates clinical rotation with clinical agency and clinical adjuncts Teaches 12 credits per semester, includes theory, clinical, skills lab and simulation lab Participate in ongoing course and curriculum revision Service: Provides engaged service at the programmatic, School, University and community levels Participates in course and programmatic assessment activities Participates in community and professional activities Participates in student recruitment and retention activities Advises currently enrolled and perspective students Scholarship: Maintains appropriate scholarly and professional development activities Provides expertise in the area of medical-surgical nursing Leadership: Contributes to the continuing innovation and development of the programs in the School of Nursing Participates in the assessment, evaluation, and accreditation of the School of Nursing programs and the University Participates in, manage, or lead projects within the School of Nursing, and University as requested Performs related duties as necessary and as assigned. Minimum Required Education Masters of Science in Nursing (required or near completion) Doctoral degree in nursing preferred Required Licenses and/or Certifications Unencumbered license as a Registered Professional Nurse in WV Required Licenses Certs Summary Unencumbered license as a Registered Professional Nurse in WV Minimum Required Qualifications - Minimum of two (2) years recent acute care experience with a focus in medical-surgical nursing, ICU , mental health, e.g. - Proficiency with Microsoft Office Required Quals Summary - Minimum of two (2) years recent acute care experience with a focus in medical-surgical nursing, ICU , mental health, e.g. - Proficiency with Microsoft Office Preferred Qualifications - Doctorate degree - Previous teaching experience in the classroom, skills and simulation lab - Experience with assessment and national accreditation - Ability to work in a collaborative environment - Familiarity with Blackboard Learning Management System - Familiarity with on-line learning - Ability to foster student learning through innovative teaching modalities - Ability to develop and maintain partnerships within the University, clinical agencies and profession - Commitment to the University and School of Nursing mission Posting Detail Information Requisition Number 2026048FP Number of Vacancies 1 Anticipated Hire Date ASAP Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 08/11/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Applicant Instructions Advertising Summary Quicklink for Posting https://www.fairmontstatejobs.com/postings/11675 Job Duties Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Certification/License Transcript #1 Transcript #2 Transcript #3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Contact Us For questions relating to Faculty/Staff positions, please e-mail the Human Resources Office at HR@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4111. For questions relating to Student Employment, please e-mail the Student Employment Office at studentjobs@fairmontstate.edu or call (304) 367-4836. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
